IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), Part IV: the elections between the two methods of treating earnings, under
-- Pilot Project No. 18 (reg 77.96), No. 19 (reg 77.98) and No. 20 (reg 77.991). Piece er5, LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Every `src:N` is a line of SOR-96-332.txt. The text is an unofficial rendering; nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- A claimant who had earnings treated under reg 77.94(3) (the larger allowable earnings of Pilot Project No. 17) may elect to keep that method instead of the 50% deduction of the pilot project of the
-- period (77.95(3), 77.97(3) or 77.99(3), in er5-pilot-earnings). The three regs have the same shape: who may elect, the deadline for telling the Commission, late elections for good cause, what happens
-- if there is no election, and finality of the Commission's decisions. Rules the text states in the same words more than once (the late election, the method that results) are stated once and cite every place.
-- All three projects are spent. Relations (Hohfeld): the claimant's power to elect (the Commission is subject to it); the Commission's immunity from appeal or reconsideration of its decision on an election
-- (the claimant's disability); the claimant's duty to inform the Commission by the deadline.
--
-- Forks: F-reg77.96a (the deadline of 77.96(3) when notifications fall under both (a) and (b)); F-reg77.96b ((5) is read as a bar, as (7) "Despite subsection (5)" implies);
-- F-reg77.96c (the end of "until March 31, 2013" is read as inclusive); F-reg77.991a (reg 77.991(2) has no condition of earlier earnings, as 77.96(2) and 77.98(2) do: read literally).

§ `Regulations Part IV - Pilot Projects: elections between the methods of treating earnings`

§§ `Words shared by regs 77.96, 77.98 and 77.991`

-- The two methods an election chooses between: the method of subsection 77.94(3) (the allowable earnings of Pilot Project No. 17), and the 50% deduction of the pilot project that applies in the period.
-- src:1529 | (2) A claimant who had earnings that were subject to subsection 77.94(3) during the period beginning on August 7, 2011 and ending on August 4, 2012 may elect to have subsection 77.94(3), instead of subsection 77.95(3), apply to earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in a benefit period, or the portion of a benefit period, that falls within the period beginning on August 5, 2012 and ending on August 1, 2015. The election is irrevocable.
-- src:1550 | (2) A claimant may elect to have subsection 77.94(3), instead of subsection 77.97(3), apply to earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in a benefit period, or the portion of a benefit period, that falls within the period beginning on August 2, 2015 and ending on August 6, 2016 if the claimant
-- src:1570 | (2) A claimant may elect to have subsection 77.94(3), instead of subsection 77.99(3), apply to earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in a benefit period, or the portion of a benefit period, that falls within the period beginning on August 7, 2016 and ending on August 11, 2018.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.96(2), reg 77.98(2), reg 77.991(2) (src:1529) (src:1550) (src:1570)
DECLARE `er5 Method of treating earnings under the pilot projects` IS ONE OF
    `er5 the allowable earnings method of subsection 77.94(3)`
    `er5 the 50 percent deduction method of the pilot project for the period`

-- Who has the method of subsection 77.94(3): a claimant who may elect, who did elect, whose election is considered made by the deadline, and who is not bound by a failure to elect for an earlier benefit period;
-- everyone else has the 50% deduction. A claimant who does not elect by the deadline has the 50% deduction (77.96(5), 77.98(7)); 77.991 has no such rule, and the 50% deduction of 77.99(3) is the project's own method.
-- src:1529 | (2) A claimant who had earnings that were subject to subsection 77.94(3) during the period beginning on August 7, 2011 and ending on August 4, 2012 may elect to have subsection 77.94(3), instead of subsection 77.95(3), apply to earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in a benefit period, or the portion of a benefit period, that falls within the period beginning on August 5, 2012 and ending on August 1, 2015. The election is irrevocable.
-- src:1534 | (5) Subject to subsection (6), if no election is made by the applicable deadline, subsection 77.95(3) applies in respect of earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in the benefit period in question and earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in any subsequent benefit period. If a benefit period ends after August 1, 2015, subsection 77.95(3) applies only in respect of earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in the portion of that benefit period that falls within the period beginning on August 5, 2012 and ending on August 1, 2015.
-- src:1550 | (2) A claimant may elect to have subsection 77.94(3), instead of subsection 77.97(3), apply to earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in a benefit period, or the portion of a benefit period, that falls within the period beginning on August 2, 2015 and ending on August 6, 2016 if the claimant
-- src:1557 | (7) Subject to subsection (8), if no election is made by the applicable deadline, subsection 77.97(3) applies in respect of earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in the benefit period in question and earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in any subsequent benefit period. If a benefit period ends after August 6, 2016, subsection 77.97(3) applies only in respect of earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in the portion of that benefit period that falls within the period beginning on August 2, 2015 and ending on August 6, 2016.
-- src:1570 | (2) A claimant may elect to have subsection 77.94(3), instead of subsection 77.99(3), apply to earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in a benefit period, or the portion of a benefit period, that falls within the period beginning on August 7, 2016 and ending on August 11, 2018.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.96(2), reg 77.96(5), reg 77.98(2), reg 77.98(7), reg 77.991(2) (src:1529) (src:1534) (src:1550) (src:1557) (src:1570)
GIVEN `the claimant may elect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant elects to have subsection 77.94(3) apply instead` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the election is considered to have been made by the deadline` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a failure to elect for an earlier benefit period binds the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `er5 Method of treating earnings under the pilot projects`
DECIDE `reg 77.96(2), (5), reg 77.98(2), (7) and reg 77.991(2) the method of treating the earnings of the benefit period` IS
    IF     `the claimant may elect`
       AND `the claimant elects to have subsection 77.94(3) apply instead`
       AND `the election is considered to have been made by the deadline`
       AND (NOT `a failure to elect for an earlier benefit period binds the claimant`)
    THEN `er5 the allowable earnings method of subsection 77.94(3)`
    ELSE `er5 the 50 percent deduction method of the pilot project for the period`

-- The portion of a benefit period that falls within a period: from the later of the two first days to the earlier of the two last days, or NOTHING when they do not overlap.
-- The election, and the 50% deduction when there is none, apply to the earnings of that portion only.
-- src:1529 | (2) A claimant who had earnings that were subject to subsection 77.94(3) during the period beginning on August 7, 2011 and ending on August 4, 2012 may elect to have subsection 77.94(3), instead of subsection 77.95(3), apply to earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in a benefit period, or the portion of a benefit period, that falls within the period beginning on August 5, 2012 and ending on August 1, 2015. The election is irrevocable.
-- src:1534 | (5) Subject to subsection (6), if no election is made by the applicable deadline, subsection 77.95(3) applies in respect of earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in the benefit period in question and earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in any subsequent benefit period. If a benefit period ends after August 1, 2015, subsection 77.95(3) applies only in respect of earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in the portion of that benefit period that falls within the period beginning on August 5, 2012 and ending on August 1, 2015.
-- src:1550 | (2) A claimant may elect to have subsection 77.94(3), instead of subsection 77.97(3), apply to earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in a benefit period, or the portion of a benefit period, that falls within the period beginning on August 2, 2015 and ending on August 6, 2016 if the claimant
-- src:1557 | (7) Subject to subsection (8), if no election is made by the applicable deadline, subsection 77.97(3) applies in respect of earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in the benefit period in question and earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in any subsequent benefit period. If a benefit period ends after August 6, 2016, subsection 77.97(3) applies only in respect of earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in the portion of that benefit period that falls within the period beginning on August 2, 2015 and ending on August 6, 2016.
-- src:1570 | (2) A claimant may elect to have subsection 77.94(3), instead of subsection 77.99(3), apply to earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in a benefit period, or the portion of a benefit period, that falls within the period beginning on August 7, 2016 and ending on August 11, 2018.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.96(2), reg 77.96(5), reg 77.98(2), reg 77.98(7), reg 77.991(2) (src:1529) (src:1534) (src:1550) (src:1557) (src:1570)
GIVEN `the benefit period` IS A `Period of days`
      `the period` IS A `Period of days`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Period of days`
DECIDE `er5 reg 77.96 the portion of the benefit period that falls within the period` IS
    IF (`er5 reg 77.96 the later of two days` (`the benefit period`'s `first day of the period`) (`the period`'s `first day of the period`))
           AT MOST (`er5 reg 77.96 the earlier of two days` (`the benefit period`'s `last day of the period`) (`the period`'s `last day of the period`))
    THEN JUST (`Period of days` OF
                   (`er5 reg 77.96 the later of two days` (`the benefit period`'s `first day of the period`) (`the period`'s `first day of the period`)),
                   (`er5 reg 77.96 the earlier of two days` (`the benefit period`'s `last day of the period`) (`the period`'s `last day of the period`)))
    ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `er5 reg 77.96 the later of two days` IS
    IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A DATE
      b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `er5 reg 77.96 the earlier of two days` IS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

-- (4) of 77.96, (6) of 77.98 and (6) of 77.991, word for word: if a claimant informs the Commission of their election after the deadline, it is considered to have been made by the deadline if the claimant shows
-- that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period from the day the deadline expired to the day the claimant informs the Commission. Whether good cause is shown is the Commission's judgment: a BOOLEAN input.
-- With no deadline determined (NOTHING) the text gives no deadline to be late for, and an election that has been made is not covered (NOTHING); an election never made is not made by any deadline.
-- src:1533 | (4) If a claimant informs the Commission of their election after the applicable deadline, the election is considered to have been made by that deadline if the claimant shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period beginning on the day on which the deadline expired and ending on the day on which the claimant informs the Commission of their election.
-- src:1556 | (6) If a claimant informs the Commission of their election after the day on which the deadline expires, the election is considered to have been made by that deadline if the claimant shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period beginning on the day on which the deadline expired and ending on the day on which the claimant informs the Commission of their election.
-- src:1574 | (6) If a claimant informs the Commission of their election after the day on which the deadline expires, the election is considered to have been made by that deadline if the claimant shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period beginning on the day on which the deadline expired and ending on the day on which the claimant informs the Commission of their election.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.96(4), reg 77.98(6), reg 77.991(6) (src:1533) (src:1556) (src:1574)
GIVEN `the day on which the claimant informs the Commission of their election, if they do` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the deadline` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the claimant shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period beginning on the day on which the deadline expired and ending on the day on which the claimant informs the Commission of their election` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.96(4), reg 77.98(6) and reg 77.991(6) the election is considered to have been made by the deadline` IS
    CONSIDER `the day on which the claimant informs the Commission of their election, if they do`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN JUST informed THEN
        CONSIDER `the deadline`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST dl THEN
            JUST (informed AT MOST dl OR `the claimant shows that there was good cause for the delay throughout the period beginning on the day on which the deadline expired and ending on the day on which the claimant informs the Commission of their election`)

-- "Whichever is earlier": 30 days after the day the last notification is issued, or the closing day of the project. Counted as the keel counts (the last day of n days after d is d plus n; that day counts).
-- src:1555 | (5) A claimant must inform the Commission of their election, if any, in respect of earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in a given benefit period not later than 30 days after the day on which the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of one or more weeks of unemployment included in that benefit period is issued to the claimant or August 6, 2016, whichever is earlier. The election is irrevocable.
-- src:1573 | (5) A claimant must inform the Commission of their election, if any, in respect of earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in a given benefit period not later than the 30th day after the day on which the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of one or more weeks of unemployment included in that benefit period is issued to the claimant or August 11, 2018, whichever is earlier. The election is irrevocable.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.98(5), reg 77.991(5) (src:1555) (src:1573)
GIVEN `the day on which the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of one or more weeks of unemployment included in the benefit period is issued to the claimant` IS A DATE
      `the closing day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `er5 reg 77.98 the earlier of 30 days after the last notification and the closing day` IS
    `er5 reg 77.96 the earlier of two days` (`the last day of` 30 `days after` `the day on which the last notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of one or more weeks of unemployment included in the benefit period is issued to the claimant`) `the closing day`

§§ `Reg 77.96 - Pilot Project No. 18, the election`

-- src:1528 | 77.96 (1) The purpose of Pilot Project No. 18 is also to test which method, the one described in subsection 77.94(3) or the one described in subsection 77.95(3), is more effective in encouraging claimants to work more while receiving benefits.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.96(1) (src:1528)
`reg 77.96(1) the purpose of Pilot Project No. 18 beyond its own` MEANS
    "test which method, the one described in subsection 77.94(3) or the one described in subsection 77.95(3), is more effective in encouraging claimants to work more while receiving benefits"

-- src:1529 | (2) A claimant who had earnings that were subject to subsection 77.94(3) during the period beginning on August 7, 2011 and ending on August 4, 2012 may elect to have subsection 77.94(3), instead of subsection 77.95(3), apply to earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in a benefit period, or the portion of a benefit period, that falls within the period beginning on August 5, 2012 and ending on August 1, 2015. The election is irrevocable.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.96(2) (src:1529)
`reg 77.96(2) the period of the earnings to which an election applies` MEANS
    `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2012 8 5), (YearMonthDay 2015 8 1)

-- (2) A claimant who had earnings that were subject to subsection 77.94(3) during the period from August 7, 2011 to August 4, 2012 may elect to have 77.94(3), instead of 77.95(3), apply to earnings received during all weeks
-- of unemployment in a benefit period, or the portion of it, that falls within the period from August 5, 2012 to August 1, 2015. The election is irrevocable.
-- src:1529 | (2) A claimant who had earnings that were subject to subsection 77.94(3) during the period beginning on August 7, 2011 and ending on August 4, 2012 may elect to have subsection 77.94(3), instead of subsection 77.95(3), apply to earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in a benefit period, or the portion of a benefit period, that falls within the period beginning on August 5, 2012 and ending on August 1, 2015. The election is irrevocable.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.96(2) (src:1529)
GIVEN `the claimant had earnings that were subject to subsection 77.94(3) during the period beginning on August 7, 2011 and ending on August 4, 2012` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.96(2) the claimant may elect` IF
    `the claimant had earnings that were subject to subsection 77.94(3) during the period beginning on August 7, 2011 and ending on August 4, 2012`

-- src:1529 | (2) A claimant who had earnings that were subject to subsection 77.94(3) during the period beginning on August 7, 2011 and ending on August 4, 2012 may elect to have subsection 77.94(3), instead of subsection 77.95(3), apply to earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in a benefit period, or the portion of a benefit period, that falls within the period beginning on August 5, 2012 and ending on August 1, 2015. The election is irrevocable.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.96(2) (src:1529)
GIVEN `the claimant has made an election` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.96(2) the election is irrevocable` IF
    `the claimant has made an election`

-- (3) The claimant must inform the Commission of their election by the applicable deadline: (a) if a notification of payment or non-payment of benefits for weeks of the benefit period is issued during the period from
-- August 5, 2012 to January 5, 2013, then February 5, 2013 or 30 days after the day the last such notification is issued, whichever is later; (b) if one is issued after January 5, 2013, then 30 days after the day the last
-- such notification is issued or August 1, 2015, whichever is earlier. Where notifications fall under both (a) and (b), (b) is applied, since its last notification is the later and the claimant's deadline moves with it (fork F-reg77.96a).
-- No notification in either period: no deadline is given (NOTHING).
-- src:1530 | (3) A claimant must inform the Commission of their election, if any, in respect of earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in a given benefit period by the applicable deadline as follows:
-- src:1531 | (a) if a notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of one or more weeks of unemployment included in that benefit period is issued to the claimant during the period beginning on August 5, 2012 and ending on January 5, 2013, February 5, 2013 or 30 days after the day on which the last notification in respect of one or more weeks of unemployment included in that benefit period is issued, whichever is later; or
-- src:1532 | (b) if a notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of one or more weeks of unemployment included in that benefit period is issued to the claimant after January 5, 2013, 30 days after the day on which the last notification in respect of one or more weeks of unemployment included in that benefit period is issued or August 1, 2015, whichever is earlier.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.96(3) (src:1530-1532)
GIVEN `a notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of one or more weeks of unemployment included in the benefit period was issued to the claimant during the period beginning on August 5, 2012 and ending on January 5, 2013` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of one or more weeks of unemployment included in the benefit period was issued to the claimant after January 5, 2013` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the last notification in respect of one or more weeks of unemployment included in the benefit period is issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `reg 77.96(3) the applicable deadline for informing the Commission of the election` IS
    IF `a notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of one or more weeks of unemployment included in the benefit period was issued to the claimant after January 5, 2013`
    THEN JUST (`er5 reg 77.96 the earlier of two days` (`the last day of` 30 `days after` `the day on which the last notification in respect of one or more weeks of unemployment included in the benefit period is issued`) (YearMonthDay 2015 8 1))
    ELSE IF `a notification of payment or non-payment of benefits in respect of one or more weeks of unemployment included in the benefit period was issued to the claimant during the period beginning on August 5, 2012 and ending on January 5, 2013`
         THEN JUST (`er5 reg 77.96 the later of two days` (YearMonthDay 2013 2 5) (`the last day of` 30 `days after` `the day on which the last notification in respect of one or more weeks of unemployment included in the benefit period is issued`))
         ELSE NOTHING

-- (5) to (7) Subject to (6), if no election is made by the deadline, 77.95(3) applies to the earnings of the benefit period in question and of any subsequent benefit period. (6) A claimant who has no earnings during the weeks of
-- the benefit period in question is not bound for a subsequent benefit period. (7) Despite (5), if a notification is issued during the period from August 5, 2012 to October 6, 2012 for weeks of a benefit period and none
-- after October 6, 2012, the claimant may, if no election was made for that benefit period, make an election for the subsequent benefit period. (5) is read as a bar on a later election, since (7) "Despite subsection (5)" gives back
-- a right to elect that (5) would otherwise take away (fork F-reg77.96b).
-- src:1534 | (5) Subject to subsection (6), if no election is made by the applicable deadline, subsection 77.95(3) applies in respect of earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in the benefit period in question and earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in any subsequent benefit period. If a benefit period ends after August 1, 2015, subsection 77.95(3) applies only in respect of earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in the portion of that benefit period that falls within the period beginning on August 5, 2012 and ending on August 1, 2015.
-- src:1535 | (6) If a claimant has no earnings during the weeks of unemployment included in the benefit period in question, the failure to make an election by the applicable deadline does not result in the application of subsection 77.95(3) in respect of earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in any subsequent benefit period.
-- src:1536 | (7) Despite subsection (5), if, during the period beginning on August 5, 2012 and ending on October 6, 2012, a notification of payment or non-payment of benefits is issued to a claimant in respect of one or more weeks of unemployment included in a benefit period and, after October 6, 2012, no additional notifications are issued to the claimant in respect of one or more weeks of unemployment included in that same benefit period, the claimant may, if no election is made in respect of earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in that benefit period, make an election in respect of earnings received during all weeks of unemployment included in the subsequent benefit period.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.96(5), reg 77.96(6), reg 77.96(7) (src:1534-1536)
GIVEN `no election was made for an earlier benefit period by the applicable deadline` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant had earnings during the weeks of unemployment included in the earlier benefit period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a notification was issued for weeks of the earlier benefit period during the period beginning on August 5, 2012 and ending on October 6, 2012, and no additional notification has been issued for that benefit period after October 6, 2012` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.96(5), (6) and (7) a failure to elect for an earlier benefit period binds the claimant for the subsequent benefit period` IF
        `no election was made for an earlier benefit period by the applicable deadline`
    AND `the claimant had earnings during the weeks of unemployment included in the earlier benefit period`
    AND (NOT `a notification was issued for weeks of the earlier benefit period during the period beginning on August 5, 2012 and ending on October 6, 2012, and no additional notification has been issued for that benefit period after October 6, 2012`)

-- (8) A decision of the Commission in respect of any matter related to an election, including the failure to make an election, is (a) until March 31, 2013, not subject to appeal under s 114 of the Act;
-- (b) on or after April 1, 2013, not subject to reconsideration under s 112 of the Act. "Until March 31, 2013" is read as through that day, which leaves no day between (a) and (b) (fork F-reg77.96c).
-- src:1537 | (8) A decision of the Commission in respect of any matter related to an election, including the failure to make an election, is
-- src:1538 | (a) until March 31, 2013, not subject to appeal under section 114 of the Act; and
-- src:1539 | (b) on or after April 1, 2013, not subject to reconsideration under section 112 of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.96(8) (src:1537-1539)
GIVEN `the day of the decision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.96(8)(a) the decision is not subject to appeal under section 114 of the Act` IF
    `the day of the decision` AT MOST (YearMonthDay 2013 3 31)

-- src:1539 | (b) on or after April 1, 2013, not subject to reconsideration under section 112 of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.96(8)(b) (src:1539)
GIVEN `the day of the decision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.96(8)(b) the decision is not subject to reconsideration under section 112 of the Act` IF
    `the day of the decision` AT LEAST (YearMonthDay 2013 4 1)

§§ `Reg 77.98 - Pilot Project No. 19, the election`

